{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind","id":1556928,"title":"What would the other splats Archmaster-equivalents look like in your mind?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-22T19:55:24-08:00","id":1556928,"title":"What would the other splats Archmaster-equivalents look like in your mind?","content":"Just curious on people's thoughts on what the other splats, if they had ever gotten an Imperial Mysteries type book, would look like with their equivalents to archmages.<br /> <br /> For mummies my thoughts would be ascending to Anpu's side and working to become a Judge or agent of Sutekh and having mummy minions of their own. For werewolf more bodhisattva types who embody the hunt fully and might hunt or be the host for a firstborn. Sin-eaters would imo be trying to fight in the underworld. I'm not sure for hunter or the other splats. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T20:49:50-08:00","id":1556929,"title":"","content":"Methuselahs and the True Fae are almost explicitly Vampire and Changeling's equivalent of archmages in terms of actors at the global scale, with Incarnate Beasts having the potential to edge into that space depending on that particulars of their Inheritance and demons likewise having the theoretical capacity to reach some sort of transcendent state depending on their vision of Hell and how effectively they pursue it.<br /> <br /> Prometheans don't really work in such a way that this question makes sense for them, though rumors about the Progenitors of Lineages fill some of the appropriate narrative space. Sin-Eaters likewise are ultimately here for a good time rather than a long time, thus the closest thing to &quot;becoming an archmaster&quot; is becoming a Chthonic God via Cabeiros \u2014 and considering that puts you in the shaky position of being something people aren't sure even exist in the strict sense, there's minimal difference between that and leaving a legacy of a successful Catabasis that leads to the Underworld working differently.<br /> <br /> Deviants are such a broad category of being and the metaphysics of their powers beyond the core principle of &quot;your soul is broken&quot; are so varied that there isn't really space for anything beyond the level of doing really well at being a deviant (maxing out Acclimation, easing your Scars in terms of both Magnitude and Scar Resistance, etc), and that same definition means most definitions of transcendence literally involve you not being a deviant anymore when the type of people most inclined to pursue that goal are creating deviants as ultimately failed test subjects for whatever procedure they're waiting to perfect before they use it on themselves.<br /> <br /> Hunters don't really have anything that works as an archmaster equivalent for obvious reasons, and while the nature of most conspiracies means the closest equivalent is whatever supernatural elements might be pulling the strings or compromising the principles of the Vigil for their agents, the nature of the gameline means similar problems to Deviant crop up.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't strictly fit the &quot;global-scale magical-political actor&quot; model of archmaster-likes, though the occasional &quot;bodhisattva predator&quot; sorts alluded to within the line fit the headspace of &quot;legendary being&quot; Promethean accords to the Progenitors.<br /> <br /> The Arisen either don't have archmaster equivalents or have the various subtypes of Apotheosis described in 2e, depending on your definition, because that's what happens when the gameline's genesis points include a sticky note that says &quot;Fuck it, you start out as the Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a more particular metric we're using to define &quot;archmaster equivalent&quot;? Because the broad strokes of the archetypes that come to mind are fairly splat-agnostic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T09:53:40-08:00","id":1556935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1556929#post1556929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methuselahs and the True Fae are almost explicitly Vampire and Changeling's equivalent of archmages in terms of actors at the global scale, with Incarnate Beasts having the potential to edge into that space depending on that particulars of their Inheritance and demons likewise having the theoretical capacity to reach some sort of transcendent state depending on their vision of Hell and how effectively they pursue it.<br /> <br /> Prometheans don't really work in such a way that this question makes sense for them, though rumors about the Progenitors of Lineages fill some of the appropriate narrative space. Sin-Eaters likewise are ultimately here for a good time rather than a long time, thus the closest thing to &quot;becoming an archmaster&quot; is becoming a Chthonic God via Cabeiros \u2014 and considering that puts you in the shaky position of being something people aren't sure even exist in the strict sense, there's minimal difference between that and leaving a legacy of a successful Catabasis that leads to the Underworld working differently.<br /> <br /> Deviants are such a broad category of being and the metaphysics of their powers beyond the core principle of &quot;your soul is broken&quot; are so varied that there isn't really space for anything beyond the level of doing really well at being a deviant (maxing out Acclimation, easing your Scars in terms of both Magnitude and Scar Resistance, etc), and that same definition means most definitions of transcendence literally involve you not being a deviant anymore when the type of people most inclined to pursue that goal are creating deviants as ultimately failed test subjects for whatever procedure they're waiting to perfect before they use it on themselves.<br /> <br /> Hunters don't really have anything that works as an archmaster equivalent for obvious reasons, and while the nature of most conspiracies means the closest equivalent is whatever supernatural elements might be pulling the strings or compromising the principles of the Vigil for their agents, the nature of the gameline means similar problems to Deviant crop up.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't strictly fit the &quot;global-scale magical-political actor&quot; model of archmaster-likes, though the occasional &quot;bodhisattva predator&quot; sorts alluded to within the line fit the headspace of &quot;legendary being&quot; Promethean accords to the Progenitors.<br /> <br /> The Arisen either don't have archmaster equivalents or have the various subtypes of Apotheosis described in 2e, depending on your definition, because that's what happens when the gameline's genesis points include a sticky note that says &quot;Fuck it, you start out as the Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a more particular metric we're using to define &quot;archmaster equivalent&quot;? Because the broad strokes of the archetypes that come to mind are fairly splat-agnostic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking mostly of in terms of characters who in a normal game would be plot devices, but now you get to play as one and see the wars and games they fight above the normal level. Vampire Methuslashs are the most obvious for high end style, since we've probably got the most support for that in game. <br /> <br /> I agree with changeling high ends becoming true fae and its fitting for them and fits (imo) with archmasters burning all ties to mortal life for that power and the cost of the power.<br /> <br /> That's true on Sin-eaters, though I feel something like trying to be remembered and leaving an impact that the dead will remember when you burn out could be something.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T19:10:53-08:00","id":1556944,"title":"","content":"Acrozatarim shared some of his basic ideas for the bodhisattva predators of werewolves and how they would work out. I think it was mostly on Discord but the core idea was no matter who you are or what you are &quot;the wolf is in the room.&quot; The idea being that as predators of that class they are a danger to the existence of things that don't normally have to worry about mundane issues like getting hit by a car. They bring that with them.<br /> <br /> The hunt is the hunt, it's just more abstract when you're hunting archmages and shadow gods. Like in Fall of Cthulhu, or Shakara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2025, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T00:54:39-08:00","id":1556955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1556935#post1556935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking mostly of in terms of characters who in a normal game would be plot devices, but now you get to play as one and see the wars and games they fight above the normal level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>'s observations apply well to this.<br /> <br /> Mummy work on the principle that this is already your initial state. So much so that apotheosis actually reduces your power instead of increasing it. The closest you can get to it would be a Mummy that somehow got to greatly increase their time at each Sekhem level. Becoming a Judge or something would mean becoming a fundamentally distinct splat, which isn't exactly the idea as I understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T07:56:08-08:00","id":1557177,"title":"","content":"The one time I STd an Imperial Mysteries game the antagonists were another archmage, Mordred, a true fae/old gods of Arcadia, and the g'd-machine itself. So maybe that indicates the kind of power scale you are thinking of. Rank 5+ Spirits were also involved as NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T08:08:15-08:00","id":1557179,"title":"","content":"I also just had a thought. I know BtP is not everyone's favorite game. But a Hero (one of the antagonists in the game) is essentially a Hunter who has transcended mere mortality. I think a game playing Heroes would actually be more interesting than a straight BtP game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T09:24:34-08:00","id":1557182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557179#post1557179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also just had a thought. I know BtP is not everyone's favorite game. But a Hero (one of the antagonists in the game) is essentially a Hunter who has transcended mere mortality. I think a game playing Heroes would actually be more interesting than a straight BtP game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes have not transcended mortality and their role as antagonists is closer to the life-sabotage model occupied by Huntsmen, the Strix, and subtler sorts of idigam. They heal a little faster than normal and develop Gifts that give them an edge in combat with Beasts in particular, but the going theory for a Heroic counterpart to an Incarnate is one that's killed over a dozen Beasts when Beasts are not commonplace.<br /> <br /> They also aren't the same thing as hunters at all, as the corebook directly highlights at multiple points \u2014 the standard antagonist Hero mindset is, not to put too fine a point on it, homicidally obsessed with Beasts, and operating on the form of moral code that hunters generally take a long time on the Vigil to warp their Integrity into to justify killing things that often look and act like people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T09:41:06-08:00","id":1557184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557182#post1557182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes have not transcended mortality and their role as antagonists is closer to the life-sabotage model occupied by Huntsmen, the Strix, and subtler sorts of idigam. They heal a little faster than normal and develop Gifts that give them an edge in combat with Beasts in particular, but the going theory for a Heroic counterpart to an Incarnate is one that's killed over a dozen Beasts when Beasts are not commonplace.<br /> <br /> They also aren't the same thing as hunters at all, as the corebook directly highlights at multiple points \u2014 the standard antagonist Hero mindset is, not to put too fine a point on it, homicidally obsessed with Beasts, and operating on the form of moral code that hunters generally take a long time on the Vigil to warp their Integrity into to justify killing things that often look and act like people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting. So how have you used heroes in your Beast games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-01T17:21:33-08:00","id":1557194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557184#post1557184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Interesting. So how have you used heroes in your Beast games?</div> </div> </div> </div>The standard ways for Heroes to be used in Beast are either as a potential risk explaining why what passes for Begotten society doesn't linger at the Starving level of Satiety or as an actual threat in terms of shifting the predominant narrative surrounding them to &quot;the Beast needs to be killed (by a Hero).&quot; The former is accomplished by the fact that being at Low Satiety attracts Heroic attention and getting back above that level makes a Beast vulnerable to Anathema that then need maxed-out or zeroed-out Satiety to clear; the latter adds Heroes' ability to recruit followers to further arm themselves and steer the confrontation within the mortal sphere as a prelude to or substitute for direct confrontation in or around the Lair.<br /> <br /> They can be smart or foolish in how they go about it, but the type of Hero that serves as an antagonist in a Beast chronicle is one that is driven to kill the Begotten and derive Primordial power from their murder. Generally speaking, the &quot;transcendence&quot; options for Heroes are getting out of the game or the alluded-to storied existence that extends their natural lifespan in service to that drive after passing a certain threshold of success. Heroes reaching the famed status of Heracles and the like is, at best, in the same section of &quot;legendary actors&quot; as I mentioned for werewolves, Prometheans, and deviants \u2014 their Gifts function solely in relation to making things difficult for Beasts and their kin, and while their influence in a story may get to be very extensive indeed it's not substantially different from what a magically persuasive monster or even a normal human with a lot of luck can accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T13:16:44-08:00","id":1557321,"title":"","content":"I've been (slooooowly) working on an idea for werewolves. Something that turns them into the equivalents of Rank 6+ spirits, embodying some primordial aspect of predation. Gods of the Hunt. A lot of the ideas are still loose, but I realize, there are a <i>lot </i>of things that need hunting even at the god-tiers: Fae, actual gods and spirits, Abyssal entities, and weirder one-off things like the ones at the end of the <i>Predators </i>book but souped up. If their territory becomes the Tapestry entire, or large swathes of it, then we figure they're probably out hunting some pretty crazy things. <br /> <br /> If a Rahu embodies the aspect of the killing wolf beneath the Full Moon's glare, then the &quot;archwerewolf&quot; equivalent stalks the hunting grounds where moons devour celestial impacts, where stars eat each other, the hazy lands beyond perception where ravenous things redefine &quot;ancient&quot; and warp understanding itself in their hunger. Here the Wolf hunts not for flesh and blood but to tear a new meaning, crimson and hot, into the worlds below. <br /> <br /> All very early ideas, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T19:35:49-08:00","id":1557324,"title":"","content":"For werewolves, I'd look to the likes of Father Wolf and the First Pack, but in the context of (if I recall correctly) the <i>To the Strongest </i>Dark Era: the one that existed before the modern Gauntlet came into existence and when there was a liminal zone between the physical and spiritual worlds inhabited by beings that were a blend of both. I forget what they were called; &quot;Pangaeans of the Border Marches&quot;, I think? <br /> <br /> The idea would be that you would need to somehow regain that &quot;middle ground&quot; state as a prerequisite to becoming a Predator of Legends. Your part-spirit nature should then give you a Spirit Rank that's not just a matter of which spirits defer to you, but an actual measure of how powerful your spirit-like qualities are. This Rank can then be increased in some manner until it exceeds 5, at which point you're in the realm of being a godlike Pangaean who potentially operates on the same stage as the First Pack. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm not as deeply versed in WtF lore as I could be; so its possible that what I just said is nonsense. In which case, please disregard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T21:19:13-08:00","id":1557327,"title":"","content":"One thing I might ask is how do you compare a super splat that literally accesses the source code of existence to anything else that cannot do the same thing. The Supernal influences everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28961-sabelforge","name":"Sabelforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28961_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T22:43:51-08:00","id":1557328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557327#post1557327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I might ask is how do you compare a super splat that literally accesses the source code of existence to anything else that cannot do the same thing. The Supernal influences everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly by that access being pretty tightly constrained. Actual visits to the Supernal cost Willpower dots and risk Aponoia, Imperial spells take Quintessences, and their less limited abilities are significantly not unique within their tier of power.<br /> <br /> Simply having freedom from some of the limitations of normal PC monsters and greater influence and/or magical potency or durability goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T13:05:09-08:00","id":1557425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557324#post1557324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For werewolves, I'd look to the likes of Father Wolf and the First Pack, but in the context of (if I recall correctly) the <i>To the Strongest </i>Dark Era</div> </div> </div> </div>To The Strongest was the one set during the beginning of the Hellenistic era, named for Alexander the Great's purported last words.<br /> <br /> The one set in the world just prior to the Sundering is called The Sundered World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">forget what they were called; &quot;Pangaeans of the Border Marches&quot;, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally just Pangaeans, as Pangaea is presented as corresponding to the original name of the Border Marches that later Uratha mythology will disperse into describing the paradisical pre-Sundered world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T13:05:46-08:00","id":1557426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557327#post1557327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I might ask is how do you compare a super splat that literally accesses the source code of existence to anything else that cannot do the same thing. The Supernal influences everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Below, So Above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T18:45:28-08:00","id":1557431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557327#post1557327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I might ask is how do you compare a super splat that literally accesses the source code of existence to anything else that cannot do the same thing. The Supernal influences everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris Allen's stat blocks for the Pangeans has them having the equivalent of supernal magics in power. Wolf was the ultimate hunter, their firstborn are all greater spirit gods, why wouldn't a uratha of extreme power not be able to be able to hunt anything or anywhere by becoming more spirit than human? Even on a golden road? The Uratha are God-killers, they murdered the avatar of an entire realm and were made to be the bane of gods. <br /> <br /> And that's not touching the fact that if we go by IM, <i>no one</i> has ever undone the first change of an uratha. Warden Moon is an incredibly powerful spirit with eons of experince and Helios likely to get involved to. And IM also has mentions of the old gods of the thistile, aka, the true fae, as capturing archmasters and hollowing them out and turning them into lures and traps. Those things might not be able to beat an exarch but if they can <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T20:43:41-08:00","id":1557440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557431#post1557431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chris Allen's stat blocks for the Pangeans has them having the equivalent of supernal magics in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is previously established as part of their rules in the Sundered World.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras, p58, &quot;As well as Influences and Numina, a Pangaean also possesses Arcana dots equal to its Rank. It casts spells using its Rank instead of Gnosis. Many Pangaeans also possess other unique powers over the world.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T12:03:29-08:00","id":1557474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557327#post1557327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I might ask is how do you compare a super splat that literally accesses the source code of existence to anything else that cannot do the same thing. The Supernal influences everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557426#post1557426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Below, So Above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The relationship between Supernal and Phenomenal (a.k.a. Fallen) is a two-way street, as described in IM. That's the whole reason why archmasters have to arrange for changes to the Phenomenal World that approximate the Supernal change that they want to make, and why the part that's done in the Supernal is more a matter of &quot;locking in the changes&quot; than anything else. <br /> <br /> That said, I wasn't aware we were talking about &quot;creatures that can interfere with works of Imperium&quot;. That's a very <b>Mage</b>-specific issue. What was being discussed, to my understanding, was &quot;endgames&quot; for non-<b>Mage</b> gamelines that allow the protagonists to acquire godlike power. Werewolves becoming Pangaians would certainly qualify, as would changelings becoming Gentry. I'm not much into <b>Vampire</b>, so I can't say if <b>Requiem</b>'s elders are like <b>Masquerade</b>'s Methuselahs in this regard (I seem to recall something about Torpor causing a diminishing of the vampire, and a Fog of Ages robbing the Elders of their vast centuries of experience; but that was back in 2004, and a lot has changed since then); but if they are, then they'd also be an example of this. <br /> <br /> Whether or not they can interfere with archmasters messing with &quot;reality's source code&quot; is a separate issue. IM indicates that there are non-mages who can and do interfere on behalf of the other gamelines; but it doesn't say that those beings are something that protagonists of those gamelines can become. Prometheans have an endgame of becoming human; but they also have in their cosmology the Principle and the <i>qashmallim</i>. And while the Principle stands for Promethean cosmology when an archmaster attempts to redefine reality, that doesn't mean that a Promethean can become anything like the Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T12:34:02-08:00","id":1557476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557474#post1557474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves becoming Pangaians would certainly qualify</div> </div> </div> </div>Pangaeans aren't something a character could become without an extreme change to the worldstate, not least because Pangaea no longer exists and every remaining Pangaean has either died off or turned into something else to adapt to that change \u2014 the original Pangaeans were made of flesh with a stone heart whose presence within any remains allowed them to gradually revive from death, but the value of those divine soul-stones and the fact that the natural weapons of werewolves count as a Bane to all Pangaeans mean even if the fall of the Border Marches didn't wrench spirits out of the Flesh and render horrible fates to former Claimed, the pressure to evolve or die was very real for them when the Sundering happened seven thousand years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not much into <b>Vampire</b>, so I can't say if <b>Requiem</b>'s elders are like <b>Masquerade</b>'s Methuselahs in this regard (I seem to recall something about Torpor causing a diminishing of the vampire, and a Fog of Ages robbing the Elders of their vast centuries of experience; but that was back in 2004, and a lot has changed since then); but if they are, then they'd also be an example of this. </div> </div> </div>2e has not strictly provided an update to Methuselahs from 1e, but they were distinguished from other ancients by their Blood Potency not diminishing with time spent in torpor and their memories consistently not being subject to the Fog of Eternity; the one example with a statblock has a high-Blood Potency Devotion that allows him to roll to fiat plot complications into existence to steer destiny toward a declared target outcome, and a likely candidate for a second example in the fiction has three bodies at once (both characters underwent a death as a vampire that seems to have served as a &quot;second Embrace&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T17:45:16-08:00","id":1557489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557476#post1557476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pangaeans aren't something a character could become without an extreme change to the worldstate, not least because Pangaea no longer exists and every remaining Pangaean has either died off or turned into something else to adapt to that change \u2014 the original Pangaeans were made of flesh with a stone heart whose presence within any remains allowed them to gradually revive from death, but the value of those divine soul-stones and the fact that the natural weapons of werewolves count as a Bane to all Pangaeans mean even if the fall of the Border Marches didn't wrench spirits out of the Flesh and render horrible fates to former Claimed, the pressure to evolve or die was very real for them when the Sundering happened seven thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe instead like a Firstborn or super spirit then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T18:35:11-08:00","id":1557491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556928-what-would-the-other-splats-archmaster-equivalents-look-like-in-your-mind?p=1557489#post1557489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe instead like a Firstborn or super spirit then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn are half-Pangaeans who became full spirits and occupy a nebulous line of transition from &quot;All Pangaeans are at least Rank 3 and usually Rank 5 or higher&quot; to &quot;the tribal totems of the Forsaken and Pure Tribes are Rank 7&quot; by virtue of those coming from different books in the franchise. Tribes of the Moon included a couple concepts like Milestone Gifts and Red Wolf's avatars the Lucky Seven, and the descriptions of how Hunter's Aspects work for the Pure indicate that the notion of becoming closer to your tribal patron remains a valid means of moving up the ladder in terms of narrative scope, but pretty much by definition that's going to have hard limits barring some means of usurping the position of Example Wolf at some point, especially if you have to take a detour into becoming a spirit (for which a loose comparison can be made to a demon becoming a powerful exile, gaining Rank through their Parameters, and subverting some major piece of Infrastructure, or a Bale Hound becoming one of the Maeladar and climbing the infernal hierarchy).<br /> <br /> So, given that their natural (or at least established) framework precludes their getting to the same tier of activity as the gods, anything the Uratha might become at that level is kind of off the roadmap by design. The Cull's enlightenments from Shunned by the Moon point to some legendary powers, and lodges potentially reaching the scope of tribes might result in a totem with a greater personal stake in your personal success, but just as there's a power gap between &quot;legendary Court founder/blazon-bearer&quot; and &quot;True Fae,&quot; anything a werewolf can become that breaks the threshold of &quot;extremely powerful magical shapeshifter&quot; is going to have to go through some semi-unique break from the norms of their operating framework \u2014 and the Shadow is an extremely flexible and durable framework when not dealing with the alien or the atrocious; cannibalism seems to be the best candidate by far without becoming a Bale Hound, messing with the Void, or otherwise tapping into forces beyond the usual currents of Essence between Flesh and Shadow.<br /> <br /> Like Data says, not every splat lends itself to Ascension War advocates who are part of the continuum of PC monsters, and a lot of the ones that do have them as a failstate or a chronicle's end goal. Getting a PC to the level of a Tier Four game is often going to involve building the road as you go, especially for gamelines where that status doesn't come with a long-term plan, upward escape clause, or higher-functioning surrender to fundamental drives. Werewolves are the ground-level actors in a system Wolf set up with design input from Luna to the end of maintaining the divide between the worlds while his more powerful children were mostly left to their own devices, and even when he was alive their directive was fluid enough for Claimed to be semi-commonplace while modern werewolves make varying levels of compromise to get their territory the way they want it. Commanding the respect of gods is more a matter of Renown and political clout than abnormal extremes of magical power in that framework, but that doesn't break the framework without involving the conceits of plot devices, which are unique as a necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T10:30:50-08:00","id":1557810,"title":"","content":"I have something in mind for something that watches out for Deviants in the Ascension War, but its going on the Vault and I'm not the lead on the book, so I'm just going to have to toss a [REDACTED] at you and remember to come back here once its out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 01-21-2026, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T08:58:34-08:00","id":1557965,"title":"","content":"I have an idea of Geists becoming post-PC power level.<br /> <br /> Post-Catharsis the Geist and sin-eater become one and are typically removed from play. But treating them as Rank 6+ ghostly entities, with specific connection to either the Underworld or passing on. I'm not sure whether influences or Numina would be a good fit for describing how they would operate in play.<br /> <br /> But likely opposing the power of a Tyrant who has committed Caberios... A Chthonic God...and given the general state of the Underworld, it might be safe to assume the Chthonic Gods aren't that nice...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T20:26:25-08:00","id":1557975,"title":"","content":"*mildly contributing the most boring off hand summation on record*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1497186#post1497186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting before the list is that a specialized high end state/endgame is not always conducive to the game's ideas and themes. That said:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Elder<br /> Werewolf: Probably dead before you have to worry about this.<br /> Mage:Archmage/Ascension<br /> Promethean: Redemption<br /> Changeling: Let's not insult them by calling True Fae an Endgame.<br /> Hunter: Not-applicable.<br /> Geist: Catharsis<br /> Mummy: Apotheosis<br /> Demon: Hell<br /> Beast: Inheritance<br /> Deviant: Technically Guardian/Fury</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T05:03:20-08:00","id":1557984,"title":"","content":"To be fair, &quot;probably dead before you have to worry about this&quot; is true across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T08:05:45-08:00","id":1558094,"title":"","content":"Looking at Acro's writeup for Lycaon-Ur as a archmaster equiv feels about what I would have imagined but I def aimed to low in terms of power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, well here is one of several write-ups I have for what Lycaon-Ur might be, and the most 'traditional' in that he's not outright a spirit or angel or whatnot. It, er, horribly breaks Claire's rules in the first post (sorry Claire!) and features some ideas I have been playing around with for elder werewolves that are just my musings and in no way an indication of how official products may treat them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Lycaon-Ur</b></span><br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Ghost Wolf<br /> <b>Auspice: </b>None. Lycaon-Ur possesses a unique equivalent in the Blessing of Zeus, below.<br /> <b>Blood: </b> Alpha <b>Bone: </b>Guru <b>Vice: </b>Gluttony (yes, he has a Vice as well)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 4 Wits 5 Resolve 6<br /> Strength 6 Dexterity 4 Stamina 8<br /> Presence 6 Manipulation 5 Composure 2<br /> <br /> Academics 3 Crafts 3 Investigation 4 Medicine 2 Occult 5 Politics 4<br /> Athletics 4 Brawl 7 Stealth 6 Survival 5 Weaponry 4<br /> Animal Ken 5 Empathy 5 Expression 6 Intimidation 7 Persuasion 6 Socialise 4 Streetwise 3 Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> Allies 5 (Lodge of the Field), Dedicated Locus 5, Fortified Form 5 (Gauru, Urshul), Indomitable, Instinctive Defence 2, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Language 4, Living Weapon 5 (Urshul), Relentless Assault 4, Resources 5, Retainer 4, Safe Place 5, Staff 5, Status 5 (Lodge of the Field), Striking Looks 1, Tactical Shifting 5<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> 5 (See Stainless Harmony below)<br /> <b>Essence: </b>100/20 (See Bodhisattva Predator below)<br /> <b>Health: </b>13<br /> <b>Renown:</b> Cunning 4, Glory 4, Honor 3, Purity 3, Wisdom 4<br /> <b>Influence: </b>Hunger 5<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Death (Cold Embrace, Barghest, Bone Gnaw), Dominance(All), Elementals (Catastrophe, Tongue of Flame), Evasion (All), Insight (Prey on Weakness, Read the World\u2019s Loom, Scent the Unnatural, One Step Ahead), Stealth (Shadow Pelt, Predator\u2019s Shadow, Running Silent), Strength (All), Warding (All), Weather (Hunt Under Iron Skies), Change (All), Hunting (All), Pack (Maw of Madness). If you use the Gift of Essence from the Giver of Gifts article, Lycaon-Ur also has access to all of the Facets of that Gift.<br /> <br /> <b>Bodhisattva Predator:</b> Having transcended into something greater, Lycaon-Ur has an increased Essence Pool and Essence per turn capability. He is capable of entering the Sacred Hunt at any time without needing to perform the rite, simply gaining the Siskur-Dah Condition against a prey of his choice. He is a set part of reality and cannot be removed from it except by his death; attempts to delete Lycaon-Ur from the timeline, rewrite reality so that he is not part of it or otherwise utterly unmake him will fail.<br /> <i>Totemic Transcendence: </i>Achieved enlightenment through spiritual power, becoming a totem. Lycaon-Ur gains Influences as if he were a spirit of Rank equal to his honorary Rank, using Presence + Wits in place of Power + Finesse. He gains 3 Essence per day and 1 additional point of Influence due to serving as a totem to his Lodge. He also gains the usual capabilities of a Lodge totem to detect Lodge members, etc.<br /> <i>Enlightenments:</i> Lycaon-Ur has access to the following powers:<br /> <i>Enlightened Renown (Cunning, Glory):</i> Lycaon-Ur gains the Rote quality on all dice pools that include his Cunning or Glory Renowns.<br /> <i>Inviolate Soul:</i> Lycaon-Ur\u2019s soul cannot be damaged, tampered with or removed by anything but an idigam, and while on the Sacred Hunt no mind-influencing affects can cause him to turn from his prey.<br /> <i>Primal Form (Urshul): </i>Lycaon-Ur adds his Purity to his Strength and Size in Urshul form.<br /> <i>Radiant Flesh:</i> As well as his normal regeneration, Lycaon-Ur regenerates a single point of aggravated damage every turn.<br /> <i>Stainless Harmony: </i>Lycaon-Ur\u2019s Harmony is set at 5 and cannot change.<br /> <br /> <b>Devourer:</b> Lycaon-Ur gains twice as much Essence as normal from consuming human flesh. Doing so also heals him for a single point of lethal or bashing damage per point of Essence gained in this way, and he can remove a Tilt after consuming an entire body in this way (even a persistent Tilt). Whenever a member of the Lodge of the Field consumes human flesh, Lycaon-Ur gains a single point of Essence from the feeding. Lycaon-Ur can consume anything and draw sustenance from it without suffering any sort of detrimental effects, toxicity or the like. Anything he consumes is annihilated utterly, and his bite attack deals aggravated rather than lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Hungerer: </b>Lycaon-Ur is continually hungry and must spend a point of Essence every day that he goes without consuming human flesh. Simply by touching another character, he can cause them to gain the Gluttony Vice. A character so affected can be subject to the Claim manifestation by hunger spirits without needing to be Controlled first.<br /> <br /> <b>Clockwork Heart:</b> Lycaon-Ur is attuned to a unique object, an egg of gears and lightning that is well-hidden. If killed while still possessing Essence, Lycaon-Ur will reform around the egg like a spirit would, the egg replacing his heart. Once reformed in this way, the egg serves as a normal heart would; removing it will kill Lycaon-Ur.<br /> <br /> <b>Forge Spawn:</b> By spending 10 Essence, Lycaon-Ur can vomit out a new-born Rank 1 hunger spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Forge Hive-Claimed:</b> By spending 50 Essence, Lycaon-Ur can force a hunger spirit to bond to an existing hunger-Claimed, creating a Hive-Claimed. He may not force a spirit to bond to a Hive-Claimed that already has 10 or more spirits in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing of Zeus:</b> In place of a normal auspice, Lycaon-Ur has a unique Glory-related auspice power set from the messenger that Changed him. The first four Facets of this Gift grant him various benefits, some of which are included in the above powers; he is also immune to damage from electricity or lightning, and gains the Blast Numina (using Presence + Wits in place of Power + Finesse). If Lycaon-Ur continues to lead the Lodge of the Field to success, he will gain Glory 5 and unlock the final Facet, effect currently unknown.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}